# AccessBuddy: pickup location missing from member email

## Problem

Sue (SMLSC admin) programmed Trevor Armstrong's fob and chose the Patrol Tower as the pickup location. Trevor received the "Ready for Collection" email and it did not say Patrol Tower. Nick reports it as "the fob location was missing". The admin UI shows Patrol Tower on the request, so the stored data and the sent email disagree.

## Vision

Nick reads one explanation that names the exact line where the admin's choice is dropped, sees why the UI still shows the right location afterwards, and knows the one-line probe in the admin UI that proves it, plus the smallest fix.

## Out of Scope

No code change in this run. No production database access (background-job permission classifier denies the Cloud SQL window; see gotcha memory). No Resend forensics (send-only keys). No fix for the separate cron row-level-security finding beyond reporting it.

