- 2026-09-16: Tier E3 from classifier. Reproduce-first gate A fired but a live reproduction is blocked: prod Cloud SQL requires the gcloud IP window, which the background-job classifier denies (gotcha-automode-blocks-prod-db-window), and Resend keys are send-only. Diagnosis proceeds from code plus migration headers that document prod state; the UI probe is handed to Nick.
- 2026-09-16: Delegation floor (E3 soft floor 2) met at 1 with show-your-math: one Explore agent for the cron sweep. A second agent (qa-verify) would need prod access this job cannot obtain; a code-fix agent is out of scope because Nick asked for a diagnosis.
- 2026-09-16 refined: ISC-15 and ISC-16 reworded to conditional. Recent commits added sections to the daily summary (7317101), which suggests it still arrives, so RLS may not bind for the current app role. The primary diagnosis does not depend on this.
- 2026-09-16 Explore agent (cron sweep) result: the daily cron and daily-summary code select work on the bare `db` handle in every section except attestation expiry and resend (route.ts:226, :254), then wrap only the send in withTenant. Bare reads hit FORCE-RLS tables at route.ts:63-79 (tenant_memberships), :82 (context-free transaction, would throw on audit_log insert), :391-399 (credentials), :472-491 (fob_requests), :554-572 (credentials), :640-657 (fob_requests), :666-675 (audit_log), :712-716 (pickup_locations); email-queue.ts:49-59, :100-122, :208-257 (audit_log, email_queue); email.ts:957-1003, :1061-1073, :1144-1155 (fob_requests, credentials, admin_assignments, audit_log). If RLS binds for the app role, the effects are: no admin daily summaries, no expiry processing or warnings, no payment or pickup reminders, queue never drains, and two dedupe checks fail open. Verification for Nick: does the SMLSC admin daily summary still arrive, and do the cron response counters read non-zero.
- 2026-09-16 RootCauseAnalysis five-whys: root causes (1) member notification is welded inside transitionRequest, so the chained SET_PICKUP emails with data the admin never supplied and the correction path (set-pickup on awaiting_pickup) is structurally unable to email; (2) "first active location" is an invented default with no ORDER BY, arbitrary and can change after updates or vacuum; (3) no test asserts email location equals admin input for the combined flow. Additional findings: the split-mode "Update Location" form (admin-actions.tsx:640-672) shares the silent-update no-email gap; the LIMIT 1 query was already fixed once for missing tenant scope (2a41ce6) and ordering was not addressed. Recommended fix: carry pickupLocationId through /program so the one SET_PICKUP that emails already has the admin's choice; make the fallback deterministic or halt at PROGRAMMED; decide whether a location change on awaiting_pickup sends a pickupLocationChanged email; add the seam test; remediate affected members by querying audit entries with action update_pickup_location since 2026-04-30.

